{"name":"Instant Relief","hex":"#ede7d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"instant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very short period of time; a moment.","A single, usually precise, point in time."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Impending; imminent.","Urgent; pressing; acute."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instant"},{"term":"relief","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The removal of stress or discomfort.","The feeling associated with the removal of stress or discomfort."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A method of sculpture or other artwork in which shapes or figures protrude from a flat background.","A sculpture or other artwork made with such a method."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relief"}],"entries":[{"title":"Instant","blocks":[{"text":"In physics and the philosophy of science, instant refers to an infinitesimal interval in time, whose passage is instantaneous. In ordinary speech, an instant has been defined as \"a point or very short space of time,\" a notion deriving from its etymological source, the Latin verb instare, from in- + stare, meaning 'to stand upon or near.'"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant","wikidata":"Q16963779"},{"title":"Relief","blocks":[{"text":"Relief is a sculptural method in which the sculpted pieces remain attached to a solid background of the same material. The term relief is from the Latin verb relevare, to raise. To create a sculpture in relief is to give the impression that the sculpted material has been raised above the background plane. When a relief is carved into a flat surface of wood or stone, the field is actually lowered, leaving the unsculpted areas seeming higher. The approach requires chiselling away of the background, which can be time-intensive. On the other hand, a relief saves forming the rear of a subject, and is less fragile and more securely fixed than a sculpture in the round, especially one of a standing figure where the ankles are a potential weak point, particularly in stone. In other materials such as metal, clay, plaster stucco, ceramics or papier-mâché the form can be simply added to or raised up from the background. Monumental bronze reliefs are made by casting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Abraham_%28Gates_of_Paradise%29_01.JPG/330px-Abraham_%28Gates_of_Paradise%29_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relief","wikidata":"Q245117"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg/500px-Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg/1280px-Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg/500px-Panel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A common mixture of high and low relief, in the Roman Ara Pacis, placed to be seen from below. Low relief background.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanel_of_Tellus%2C_Ara_Pacis%2C_Rome.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg/500px-Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg/1280px-Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg/500px-Albert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A face of the high-relief Frieze of Parnassus round the base of the Albert Memorial in London. Most of the heads and many feet are completely undercut, but the torsos are \"engaged\" with the surface behind.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbert_Memorial_Friese_Facing_South_-_May_2008.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/PupienusSest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/PupienusSest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Low-relief on Roman sestertius, 238 AD","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APupienusSest.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg/500px-Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg/1280px-Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg/500px-Rock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A low-relief dating to c. 2000 BC, from the kingdom of Simurrum, modern Iraq","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARock_Relief_of_Iddin-Sin%2C_King_of_Simurrum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Amarna_Neues_05.JPG/250px-Amarna_Neues_05.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&